📋 **F-1692-1 (s1692 2026-08-12, MEASURED WHILE ANSWERING THE REFILL QUESTION WITH THE PRESCRIBED INSTRUMENT — `authorable-candidates.mjs` PRICES `planned` GOAL LEAVES, SO A FIRE-AUTHORABLE ITEM THAT LIVES ONLY AS A SUB-ITEM OF A BACKLOG RULING ROW IS INVISIBLE TO IT, AND ITS `0 fire-authorable` THEN READS AS *"THE BOARD HAS NOTHING"*. NON-BLOCKING; NO OWNER WORD OWED.)** This fire ran the instrument exactly as §2E and the memory index prescribe, and it reported **11 planned leaves, 11 priced, 0 FIRE-AUTHORABLE** (owner-gated 7 · attended-owed 3 · needs-spec 1) — a clean, honest answer to the question it asks. ⚠️ **At that same moment `tasks/BACKLOG.md:1` — the owner's CLEAN-SLATE ruling of 2026-08-12, re-priced at source by the attended session at `c7fabbd0a` — named item (iv) in as many words: _"the 29 menu-vs-door rows — fire-authorable audit follow-up after ap16-6"_.** ✓ **VERIFIED it carries no goal leaf, by alternate-name search rather than one grep (the DOESN'T-EXIST discipline):** `menu-vs-door` / `menu_vs_door` / `ap16-7` / `ap16-menu` each return **0** in `tasks/goals.json`; a bare `menu` grep there returns only unrelated hits (build menu, start menu, RF-09 menu-time prefetch); and the AP-16 spec's sole `menu` hit is Law 1's one-rulebook sentence at `specs/agent-play/ap-16-same-game-law.md:22`, not a slice. ⓘ **THE INSTRUMENT IS NOT BROKEN AND MUST NOT BE "FIXED" — it answers exactly the question it states (`N planned leaf/leaves — N priced`), and its own footer already warns _"a priced leaf is not a closed one"_.** The defect is in the READING: s1690 and s1691 each converted its `0` into **PIPELINE-DRY: all four lanes (needs spec/owner)**, which is a claim about the BOARD, not about the leaf set. This is the catalogued shape *a guard's denominator is narrower than the question* — the answer is right, the question was bigger. 💰 **AND THE COST IS NOT TODAY, IT IS THE FIRE AFTER `ap16-6` DRAINS.** Item (iv)'s gate is *"after ap16-6"*, which is running in lane