✅ **AP-15 SLICE 1 SHIPPED s1653 `909c0d7c` (drained: tsc+build+own guard+test:node-guards rc=0 293.0s, --check bite proven by manufactured defect; non-blocking F-1653-3 on eraStamp; review reviews/ap15-1-null-floor-anchors.md). AUTHORED s1650 (FIRE-AUTHORED — attended review welcome) — `tasks/lane-a-ap15-1-null-floor-anchors.md` → lane-a; goal leaf `ap15-1-null-floor-anchors` registered in the same commit.** THE NULL FLOOR: pinned idle-run anchors that measure **what the MAP gives away free**, from `specs/agent-play/ap-15-assay-of-minds.md`'s **"What ships first (cheap, in order)"** item 1. It is the artifact the spec's own Goodhart clause (law 2, *"decision economy is void where the null floor secures"*) depends on — until it exists, law 2 is unenforceable and every efficiency number the Field Book prints is unanchored. 💰 **PRICED BEFORE AUTHORING, WHICH IS THE POINT — F-1648-1 was parked one fire ago precisely because a full-corpus run reached the queue unmeasured (~9h):** measured on main `784e94f02`, sequential, **63.2 s for 17 contracts × 1 seed** (range 1.4–8.4 s), so the full corpus of **35 seeds ≈ 2.5 minutes**. ✅ **Three premises proved before a word of scope was written:** (1) **exactly 12 of the 17 bench contracts are door-servable** — which matches the spec's *"the 12 door-servable contracts"* exactly, so the spec was precise and it is `bench-seeds.json` that grew past the door; the other 5 (`e3-fairground` + the four e6) are refused by `SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` and are **already documented, not a bug** (F-DOOR-4, 2026-08-08, cured by the `door-contracts` block in `public/skill.md`) — explicitly firewalled OUT of the master; (2) **determinism verified** by running `the-claim`, `e1-baron` and `e2-hill-mine` twice each — `eventLogHash`, `waves`, `kills` **and** `timeMs` reproduced identically, which is what makes a pinned artifact and a `--check` drift mode meaningful at all; (3) the derivation must **not** be wired into any standing battery (only a millisecon