🔧 **F-1616-2 (s1616 2026-08-10, CONFIRMED BY MANUFACTURE AT THE f1614-1 DRAIN — THE NEW SPEC REWRITES A *TRACKED* `reviews/*.md` ON EVERY RUN, WHICH IS A HARD STOP IN BOTH PRE-FLIGHT TEMPLATES, AND IT HIDES WHENEVER THE LAST PROJECT AGREES WITH THE COMMITTED BYTES.)** ⚙️ **WHAT IT IS.** `e2e/advance-stream-walkthrough.spec.ts` writes `reviews/advance-stream-walkthrough.md` — a **tracked** file — every time the test runs. Both pre-flight templates in `.claude/skills/author-task/SKILL.md` (LANE **and** MAIN) end with the same sentence: *"What still STOPs: modified tracked `src/**`, `scripts/**`, `e2e/**`, `tasks/**`, `specs/**`, `reviews/*.md`."* The **FACTORY-CHURN (F-1407-1)** and **EVIDENCE-ARTIFACT (F-1266-1)** exceptions cover `artifacts/**`, `reviews/shots-*` and `.png` — **`reviews/*.md` is deliberately excluded from both.** ✅ **MANUFACTURED, NOT ARGUED (the s1299/s1300 standard — a passing check is not evidence about the failing path):** a desktop-only run of the spec on the merged tree, then `git status --short` → `` M artifacts/advance-stream-walkthrough.md`` and `` M reviews/advance-stream-walkthrough.md``. **That is the exact predicate `f1406-1` died on — 54,875 tokens for zero edits.** ⚠️ **THE NASTY PART IS WHY IT DID NOT SHOW UP IN THE RUNNER’S OWN GREEN RUN:** playwright runs projects in declared order, **mobile runs last**, and mobile’s numbers happened to reproduce the committed file byte-for-byte — the desktop arm had already written `town-return 4|6` over it and been overwritten back. **A trap that fires only when the last project disagrees is worse than one that always fires, because the board reads clean until the day it does not.** 📐 **TWO AGGRAVATIONS, BOTH STRUCTURAL.** (1) ✓ Verified across every `writeFile(` call site in `e2e/`: every other spec writes solely to `artifacts/**` or `reviews/shots-*` — **this is the only spec in the repo writing a tracked `reviews/*.md`**, so the convention exists and this is its sole exception. (2) Both projects write **the same path**, so at the 6 workers a lane shell uses (`playwright.config.ts:50`, `workers: isFireShell ? 1 : undefined`) the two project instances race on one file. ➡️ **CURE: write only `artifacts/`, under a per-project filename; keep the committed `reviews/advance-stream-walkthrough.md` as the static owner-facing record it already is.** The owner deliverable is *a record of a measurement*, not a file that must silently re-derive itself under every unrelated suite run. ✅ **AUTHORED THIS FIRE as `f1616-1` (lane-c).** **GATE: none owed to the owner.**
