tasks/BACKLOG.md:628:- 🟡 **F-1464-1 PARTIALLY CURED ON LANE-B — 1,075 → 301 HALO SUSPECTS WITH THE DENOMINATOR HELD AT 1,314; THE ORIGINAL FINDING REMAINS OPEN.** The ruled recipe safely cured **774** shipped files, including both standalones and every provably-loaded surface named by the finding: HUD Baron portrait **55.63% → 0.00%**, title emblem **99.17% → 0.00%**, and the four negative controls stayed **0.00% / 0 touching-art**. `scripts/halo-reextraction-check.mjs` re-runs the sweep without leaving tracked probe dirt, asserts the exact 301-cell held residue, and byte-compares all 774 cured files to pre-batch `89bfc10c`: **0 alpha differences, 0 fully-opaque RGB differences**. The task-specific standalone dimensions were decisive: direct **512→256** emblem and native **768→384** youngster preserve the invariant, while generic 1024 intermediates move alpha and opaque pixels. A final touched-file-only lossless recompression kept decoded pixels identical and reduced the production-PNG increase from **47.5 MiB to 14.9 MiB** versus the pre-batch build; master-derived shipped cells retain their exact repository encoding so the downscale byte gate stays green. `anim-pass-reextract --verify-downscale`: **453 byte-identical, 0 unexplained, 26 master-divergent by design**. This is deliberately not bannered CURED: the task's measured fallback fired, then the acceptance invariant found more shipped mends the 26-entry master ledger could not represent.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:629:- 🔺 **F-1470-4 (renumbered from F-1470-1 by the s1470 drain — ID collision, see reviews/f1464-1-halo-reextraction.md F-1470-2) — 301 HALO CELLS REMAIN ACROSS 15 HELD SHEETS; RE-EXTRACTING THEM TODAY REVERTS SHIPPED MENDS OR MOVES THE SILHOUETTE/OPAQUE INTERIOR.** Fork measurement on scratch 256px output found **23 pocket offenders / 36 cream blobs** across `char-baron-sheet-walk8` + `char-hero-sheet-walk8`, so their 64 cells and all 26 `assets/master-divergent.json` entries remain untouched. The strict pre-batch invariant then caught six older direct-output mend sheets omitted from that master-only ledger (`char-{bandit-thief,elder,newsie-mei,storekeeper,youngster-f,youngster-m}-sheet-walk8`, **192 cells**) and seven rounded-scale sheets (`char-hero-sheet-{side-f,back-f,front-f,side-actions-f,rotation2-f}`, `char-e9-feral_terraformer-sheet-walk8`, `ter-rail-elements`, **45 cells**). The first attempted batch named **79 violating files across 13 sheets** and was rolled back sheet-wise; no threshold was relaxed. **GATE:** each held sheet must produce 0 sweep suspects while `halo-reextraction-check.mjs` still reports byte-identical alpha + opaque RGB and the original pocket detector reports 0, or an attended eye must accept that sprite class under F-1464-1's existing second disjunct. ➡️ **REFINED s1485 BY MEASUREMENT — SEE F-1485-1 DIRECTLY BELOW. The "15 held sheets" is not one class but three, and the 45-cell rounded-scale third is curable today by a recipe measured end-to-end; it is held by a 1/255 threshold word, not by a shipped mend. This row's text stands as written (RETENTION LAW) — it is accurate about what s1470 measured, and its "301 cells" framing is what F-1485-1 narrows.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:633:- 🔺 **F-1485-1 (s1485, MEASURED — F-1470-4's 301 HELD CELLS ARE THREE CLASSES WITH THREE DIFFERENT CURES, AND THE 45-CELL ROUNDED-SCALE CLASS IS BLOCKED BY A TOOLING DEFECT, NOT BY ART.)** 🧭 **HOW I FOUND IT:** the board was dry and s1484 ranked F-1470-4 first, so before authoring anything I ran the gate's own predicate against the live corpus (F-1483-1). The row reads as one 301-cell blob whose members all "revert shipped mends or move the silhouette". **Measured, it is not.** 📐 **THE SPLIT (`artifacts/f1470-4/*`, all tracked and re-derivable in one command each):** **(A) 64 cells / 2 sheets** — `char-{baron,hero}-sheet-walk8`, the cutout-pocket fork that failed closed; genuinely eye-gated, UNCHANGED by this fire. **(B) 192 cells / 6 sheets** — the unledgered direct-output mend sheets, all `scale == 1`; UNCHANGED, not probed. **(C) 45 cells / 7 sheets** — the rounded-scale class, and the whole of this finding. 🔑 **THE DEFECT, NAMED IN CODE RATHER THAN INFERRED:** `extract-alpha.mjs:376` computes `scale = min(1, (cell * 0.86) / maxDim)` as a full double, `:412` writes it to `frames.json` as `Number(scale.toFixed(4))`, and `anim-pass-reextract.mjs:163` reads that **4dp** value back out and passes it in as `--scale`. Every re-extraction is therefore normalised at a scale wrong in the 5th decimal, resampling every cell a hair differently — which is exactly the alpha drift the strict invariant caught. ⚠️ **Sheets whose scale clamps to 1 are IMMUNE, because `min(1, …)` makes the rounding unobservable — and those are precisely the 774 that passed. The bug was invisible across 94% of the corpus by arithmetic accident, not because the pipeline was right.** ✅ **THE CURE, MEASURED END-TO-END ON ALL 45 CELLS (`artifacts/f1470-4/exact-scale-recipe.mjs`):** `maxDim` is an integer pixel count, so the original double is recoverable exactly — `maxDim = round(cell * 0.86 / shippedScale)`, then `scale = cell * 0.86 / maxDim`. Result across 7 sheets / 45 cells: **halo suspects 45 → 0 · alpha differences 0 (the silhouette provably does not move) · 117 fully-opaque pixels change RGB, every one of them by exactly 1/255.** 🚫 **THE OBVIOUS FIX IS WRONG, AND MEASURING IT IS WHAT SAVED THE RECIPE:** simply dropping `--scale` and letting the extractor auto-fit reproduces 4 sheets exactly and is **badly wrong on 3** — the halo cure shrinks the content bbox, so the auto-fit recomputes `maxDim` and renormalises the figure. `char-hero-sheet-rotation2-f` would go **0.7644 → 0.8719, drawing the hero ~14% larger than her sibling sheets**, with alpha deltas up to 255. *The auto path silently changes sprite SIZE; the recovery recipe does not.* 🔬 **INSTRUMENT VALIDATED BEFORE ITS NUMBERS WERE BELIEVED (`artifacts/f1470-4/instrument-controls.mjs`), because a green here proves nothing about a red:** control 1 — my sweep predicate reads **45/45** shipped rounded-scale cells as >5% suspects and **disagrees with the tracked sweep on 0**; control 2 — the same extract+resize+compare pipeline run against three **already-cured** sheets returns **alphaDiff 0 / opaqueRGB 0**, exactly, so the residue it reports on the held sheets belongs to the sprite and not to my reproduction. The A/B's **control arm reproduces the runner's failure** on all 7 sheets, so the hypothesis arm was measured against a known-bad baseline, not against nothing. 🔎 **AND ONE INHERITED CLAIM IS CORRECTED:** the f1464-1 master's measured note 2 states that of the RGB pixels the cure changes, **"0 are fully opaque"**. That was measured on **one sheet** (`char-baron-sheet-walk4-a`) and does not generalise — the cure moves **41 fully-opaque master pixels** across these 23 cells. It moves each by **exactly 1**, so the note's *spirit* (the interior does not move) survives intact and its *letter* does not. **A claim that is true for a reason its author never checked is still an unverified claim.** ⚖️ **WHY THIS FIRE STOPPED HERE AND AUTHORED NO MASTER:** the recipe satisfies every clause of F-1470-4's first disjunct except **"byte-identical … opaque RGB"**, which 117 pixels violate by 1/255. The f1464-1 master says in as many words that a failure of that invariant *"is a FINDING with the file named — not a threshold to relax"*, and **a fire may not relax a threshold an owner-facing gate is written on.** Running the predicate first is what revealed that a master queued today would fail its own acceptance gate — the F-1483-1 lesson, paying for itself before any tokens were spent on scope. **GATE: closes on ONE WORD — is an opaque-RGB delta of ≤1/255 acceptable when alpha is byte-identical? YES ⇒ 45 of the 301 cells are curable by a fire-authored master in a single lane shift, and (A)+(B)'s 256 cells remain the honest residue. NO ⇒ class (C) joins them at the attended eye, and this row closes as measured-and-declined.** 🚫 Do NOT "fix" this by editing `scripts/extract-alpha.mjs` — the 4dp record is what 1,314 shipped `frames.json` files already contain, and widening it would strand the recovery arithmetic that reads them.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:636:- ✅ **F-1493-2 CLOSED — THE TRIPWIRE EXISTS. Merged `5507b629` s1495** (review `reviews/f1493-2-baron-drift-pin.md`, +82 lines to `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs`, the only file touched). ⭐ **THE RUNNER DID THE HARD THING THE MASTER ASKED FOR RATHER THAN THE EASY THING THAT LOOKS THE SAME:** the master deliberately stated **no expected values** and told the runner that two disagreeing runs are a FINDING that FORBIDS a pin. It proved determinism **in-process** (both runs matched for all three contracts *before* pinning) **and cross-process (10/10 identical)**, and only then wrote the numbers — so the pin records a measured invariant, not a snapshot of one run. Pinned: `e2-hill-mine` 12 waves / 445 kills / `fnv1a32:a3b2c95e` · `e2-trestle` 12 / 448 / `fnv1a32:94275d9a` · `e2-incline` 12 / 424 / `fnv1a32:3362e2f0`. 🧪 **DRAIN EVIDENCE (gate-s1495 detached worktree, §3.0b, `--workers=1`): tsc rc=0 · build rc=0 · `test:node-guards` rc=0.** The decisive number is not the rc but the **count: 340 → 341 tests, +1 exactly, 0 fail** — with `✔ the E2 Baron fights keep their pinned outcomes (13063ms)` in the transcript, which is how this drain knows the new pin **executed** rather than silently not running (a pin that does not run is worse than no pin, because it reads as coverage). Landed by fast-forward: `git diff 5507b629 HEAD` EMPTY, `main..lane/a` EMPTY. ⓘ Wall-time budget honoured: `gr-sim.test.mjs` 68.63s → 86.04s, **+17.41s against a 30s cap**. ⚠️ Runner's own caveat, carried forward not buried: on the **Node 23** runner the file retains the documented timeout-control incompatibility (339/341, pre-existing per-test-timeout + fixture-teardown failures) — the fire shell is Node 26.4.0 where it is 341/341. That is the known interpreter split (F-1458-2), not a new red. 🟢 **F-1493-2 (declared s1493 by the author of its own cause, CONFIRMED s1494 on the merged tree — THE E2 BARON MAPS HAVE NO DRIFT TRIPWIRE).** When `ff628a132` correctly relaxed the census equality on baron contracts (`autoSecureWaveForRun` returns `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` while `twist.baron && !baronBeaten`, so the declared `secureWave` is a BYPASSED INPUT there), it removed the only thing — an accidental thing, true on 3 of 4 contracts by combat-speed coincidence — that would have noticed a baron fight getting longer. **A Hill Mine run drifting from 14 waves to 25 now passes everywhere.** 🔎 **VERIFIED BY READING, NOT INFERRED (s1494):** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` DOES hold an `e2-hill-mine` test, but it is the boot/mode one — it never advances to a terminal turn and pins only `escortDiagnostics` and the modes list; the ONLY byte-exact baron outcome pin anywhere is `e1-baron`. Three of four E2 contracts declare a baron (`e2-hill-mine`, `e2-trestle`, `e2-incline`); `e2-pressure-garden` is baron-less and keeps its strict equality, which the engine genuinely guarantees. 🎯 **NAMED CONSUMER, so a red can be priced:** the E1/E2 contracts are the seed corpus **AP-10d** is measured against — a baseline that moves silently breaks a comparison whose whole value is that the game is held fixed while the harness varies. 📦 **MASTER `lane-f1493-2-baron-drift-pin` AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s1494 to lane-a** (leaf `f1493-2-baron-drift-pin`): pin the three baron outcomes in `gr-sim.test.mjs` — where outcome pinning lives — NOT in the census, because a readiness instrument must assert what the engine GUARANTEES and re-conflating the two is what caused F-1492-1. States **no expected values** (the runner takes them from its own run and must prove determinism in-process AND cross-process first; two disagreeing runs are a FINDING that forbids any pin). Carries a **hard wall-time budget** because `gr-sim.test.mjs` is already ~55.6s of the every-fire `test:node-guards`. **GATE: closes when the pin is merged, or when a runner STOP proves determinism does not hold — either answer closes it.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:642:- 🟢 **F-1492-2 — RETIRED s1493 BY MEASUREMENT, NOT BY A RULING: THE QUESTION IS UNANSWERABLE AS POSED, AND NO OWNER WORD IS OWED.** s1492 put this on the desk as a content ruling (does Hill Mine’s declared `secureWave` follow the corrected sim 12 → 14?) and was right about the FILE but wrong about the NUMBER. s1493 read `autoSecureWaveForRun()` in **both** engines — `src/game/Game.ts:4844` (browser) and `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:325-328` (headless) — and it returns `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` while `twist.baron && !baronBeaten`. **A baron contract therefore never secures at its declared `secureWave` at all; it secures when the Baron dies.** So `er01-e2-census.spec.ts:109`’s equality `waves === contract.twist.secureWave` is structurally guaranteed on **exactly one of the four** E2 contracts (`e2-pressure-garden`, the only baron-less one) and was a **combat-speed coincidence** on the other three. Hill Mine is the unique cell with BOTH a baron and `pressureEnabled`, and it is the one that broke. Measured on the merged tree `714de7ebb` in detached `gate-s1493` (§3.0b): full census **6 passed / 2 failed**, the two being `e2-hill-mine` desktop+mobile, received **`{ calls: 0, secured: true, waves: 14 }`** — **still secured, still zero agent calls, still hash-deterministic**; only the wave the Railcar died in moved. ⛔ **Raising `secureWave` to 14 is REJECTED**: it would change no behaviour it appears to describe (the threshold is already bypassed), it would widen the sim’s tick budget (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:360`) and edit the player-facing “secured wave N” line (`src/ui/DeathOverlay.ts:341`), and it is the F-1441-3 re-pin reflex wearing a data file’s clothes. ➡️ **SUPERSEDED BY F-1493-1** (fire-authorable assertion repair, master queued). Evidence: `reviews/f1492-2-secure-wave-reframed.md`, `artifacts/s1493-f1492-2.txt`, `artifacts/s1493-census-full.txt`. Related and UNCHANGED: **F-1492-1** (the re-pin must land WITH the slice) · **F-1492-3** (Goal Registration Law) · **F-1492-4** (skill.md rot guard has no positive control).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:643:- 🟢 **F-1493-1 (s1493, MEASURED — THE E2 CENSUS ASSERTS A COMBAT-SPEED COINCIDENCE THROUGH A CONTRACT CONSTANT; REPAIR THE ASSERTION, NOT THE CONTRACT).** `e2e/er01-e2-census.spec.ts:109` ("${contract.id} census support is explicit and deterministic" — the assertion this row quoted verbatim, `expect(first).toMatchObject({ secured: true, waves: contract.twist.secureWave, calls: 0 });`, was REPAIRED at `ff628a132` and no longer exists at that coordinate; the TEST TITLE survives the repair, the assertion text did not — F-1310-1) asserts `waves === contract.twist.secureWave`, an equality the engine guarantees only where no `twist.baron` exists. The repair: keep the **strict** equality on baron-less contracts (do not weaken what is structurally guaranteed), and on baron contracts assert what the engine actually promises — `secured: true` and `waves >= secureWave`. Ships together with the six `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` re-pins, each carrying the named cause F-1441-3 requires (**the headless hero now carries the browser’s progression, so it survives longer and kills more**). **Determinism proven before any pin was prescribed:** `gr-sim.test.mjs` run **twice on the same commit** `714de7ebb`, all six failing `actual:` objects byte-identical (`artifacts/s1493-grsim.txt` vs `artifacts/s1493-grsim-2.txt`) — two disagreeing runs would have meant no pin was legitimate. ⚠️ **Must land WITH the cure (F-1492-1): the numbers do not exist without it**, so the master EXTENDS `lane/a` on top of `1e19a7d58` and **suspends the safe-dupe pre-flight by explicit authorization**, forbidding every reset/clean/pull verb in that worktree — `lane/a` correctly reads **HOLDS** and must not be refilled or reset. Master `tasks/lane-f1493-1-parity-repin.md` → `tasks/queue/lane-a/`, goal leaf `f1493-1-parity-repin`. **GATE: closes when the branch drains with `test:node-guards` rc=0 and the census 8/8 both projects.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:644:- 🟢 **F-1493-2 (s1493, DECLARED NOT FIXED — an honest coverage note that must not be read as a regression).** Once F-1493-1 lands, the census row no longer catches “a baron map got materially harder to clear”. **It never did, except by accident on 3 of 4 contracts** — the equality held only while each Baron happened to die inside its arrival wave. The coverage was imaginary on three maps and is now honestly absent on three maps rather than dishonestly present on four. A real tuning ratchet on baron clear-time would need its own row with its own declared budget: **a new deliverable, not a repair to this one.** No owner word needed; recorded so a future reader does not “restore” the equality and re-open F-1492-2.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:648:- 🟢 **F-MTS-1 (milk/twin-sockets 2026-08-06, MEASURED AND CURED — THE E5 + E6 ERA SOCKETS ARE BUILT, AND BUILDING THEM MOVED BOTH EPOCHS' BLOCKER OFF THE CONSUMER AND ONTO THE AGENT VERB LIST).** 🧭 **HOW I FOUND IT:** the shift was sent to socket E5 and E6 and admit what it could. Before authoring scope I probed whether each named consumer is CONSTRUCTIBLE under SSR — the s1475 lesson — and two of my own three probe stubs turned out defective, so every verdict below rests on a re-run with a corrected instrument. ✅ **SHIPPED:** `src/sim/DeepwaterSocket.ts` (DeepwaterClaimTile + DeepwaterArsenal) and `src/sim/AtomicSocket.ts` (WrangleSystem, epoch-wide, + E6TileConsumerSystem for Glow Mesa), both in the browser's own tick order, all three of wrangle's behavioural couplings included (`Game.ts:534`, `:2606`, `:2614`). Manifest gained 6 Deepwater rules, 4 wrangle rules on every Atomic contract, 2 tile rules on Glow Mesa — all consumer-sourced. ⛔ **`SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. Admission was attempted, measured, and REFUSED on all eight contracts** — the measurement is the deliverable. 🔬 **`e6-showroom` secures at wave 20 on both seeds, deterministically (`fnv1a32:27f4b15e` / `fnv1a32:84bc5a65`, both repeat IDENTICAL) — AND IT IS A FALSE GREEN.** With wrangle live an exhausted machine is undamageable (`Game.ts:536`) AND harmless (`:2606`) AND still alive, and `AgentGameAdapter` has no capture verb; from wave 6 all 60 living enemies are exhausted, `Balance.waves.aliveCap` is 60, and `WaveSystem.ts:536`+`:579` then refuse to spawn at all — so the win is against an empty board for fourteen waves. Admitting it would have pinned a determinism hash on a deadlock. 🚫 **`e6-glow-mesa` provably cannot terminate** (homemaker_9000 baron at wave 8 gates securing, `HomemakerBossSystem` unsocketed; both seeds overran the ceiling at wave 15 > 14). 🚫 **`e5-deepwater-claim` has no reachable secure condition:** `DredgeQueenBossSystem` calls `document.createElement` from INSTANCE FIELD INITIALIZERS (`:77-80`, helper `:736`), before its own `enabled` flag is read — it cannot be constructed outside a browser at any wiring effort, and it owns the contract's only exit. The socket COUNTS every refused boss handoff (`bossHandoffsRefused`) rather than skipping it silently. 🧪 **GATES: tsc rc=0 · `npm run build` rc=0 · er01-e5 8/8 and er01-e6 8/8 desktop+mobile, zero console · adjacent er01-e2/e3/e4/e7/e8/e9/e10 unmodified-green · CONTROL `node --test scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` 9/9 including the e1-dry-gulch outcome pins (every socket call is null-guarded, so no admitted contract's tick moved) · manifest swept across all 42 contracts / 10 epochs, ZERO leaks.** 🧬 **5 mutations, all BIT, every file restored byte-identically** (`reviews/milk-twin-sockets-evidence/milk-twin-sockets-mutation.mjs`). Review: `reviews/milk-twin-sockets.md`. Censuses rewritten: `docs/bench/e5-readiness-census.md`, `docs/bench/e6-readiness-census.md`.
