tasks/BACKLOG.md:678:🟢 **F-1410-3 (s1410, VERIFIED — `lane/e2-arsenal` IS NOW UNBLOCKED, AND THIS WAS THE ROAD IT WAS WAITING ON).** The substantive gate on the baron slice (E1 driver 5 of 5) was never its merge shape — the runner reports `git merge-tree` structurally clean, and s1400 said so too. It was that the merged tree made the escort headless run **spin forever** (F-1400-3: 99.4% CPU, immune to the caller's timeout) and that main's bench asserted `secured:true`, the side of the divergence **production does not produce** (F-1401-1). Both are now fixed by `e45cf7c5`: the driver cannot spin, and the bench asserts termination rather than success. ✓ **Verified that the re-based assertion is not vacuous in the world the ruling creates** — on a ceiling-failing run the process still exits with `signal=null` and stdout's first line still parses to `modes[0].id === "escort"`, so scope 4's load-bearing claim survives the baron's arrival. ⚠️ **lane-c HOLDS `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts` — RE-GRAFT it, never reset over the s1406 cure (`eaefdb24`).** **GATE: none — the road is clear; the baron re-land is now a graft exercise, not a diagnosis.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:687:🔺 **F-1407-1 (s1407, MEASURED — THE MAIN-SLOT PRE-FLIGHT TEMPLATE FORBIDS CHURN THE FACTORY ITSELF PRODUCES, AND THE CURE HAS EXISTED IN THE SIBLING TEMPLATE SINCE s1266).** The `f1406-1` dispatch of `20260802-225251` never reached scope 1. It stopped at its pre-flight having spent **54,875 tokens for zero edits**, reporting 26 modified tracked files under `artifacts/054/`, `artifacts/baron-presence/` and `artifacts/e2-enemies/` that belonged to no live task. ✓ **VERIFIED BY READING, not inferred:** those three directories hold **32 tracked PNGs** (`git ls-files`), every one written by `page.screenshot` inside the adjacent e2e specs a drain gate runs — `e2e/054-baron-epic.spec.ts:99` ("await page.screenshot({ path: path.join(ARTIFACT_DIR"), `e2e/e1-baron.spec.ts:32` ("const ARTIFACT_DIR = path.resolve("), `e2e/e2-enemies.spec.ts:10` ("const ARTIFACT_DIR = path.resolve("). **They were the exhaust of the s1406 drain that authored this very master**, and the runner picked the master up **one minute after that fire's handoff commit**. 🔑 **The fire that authored the master created the dirt that blocked it, inside the same fire, and no probe available to it at authoring time could have shown that** — so the defect is in the TEMPLATE, not in anyone's care. ⚠️ **The stronger form: `.claude/skills/author-task/SKILL.md`'s MAIN-slot pre-flight demanded `ZERO staged/modified TRACKED files`, a condition the factory makes false on nearly every cycle** — 6 modified tracked `logs/*` files at rest this fire, and 93 `logs/` file-entries across the last 40 commits touching `logs/`. s1406 noticed half of it and hand-waived `logs/*` in the master's prose; it did not know about `artifacts/**`. 🩹 **And the cure was already written, four lines above, in the LANE template**: the **F-1266-1 EVIDENCE-ARTIFACT EXCEPTION (s1266)** names `artifacts/**`, `reviews/shots-*` and `.png` as never-a-STOP, and its own rationale is verbatim the failure that just recurred — *"a run that STOPPED still ran playwright and still regenerated screenshots, so a stopped predecessor leaves tracked dirt that freezes its successor"*. It was landed into one of the two pre-flight templates and the main slot went 141 sessions without it. **The cured defect surviving in the sibling surface is the class**; the incident is only its latest instance. ✅ **CURED s1407 in both places:** the MAIN-slot template now carries a FACTORY-CHURN EXCEPTION naming `logs/**` and the F-1266-1 evidence classes, while leaving `src/**`, `scripts/**`, `e2e/**`, `tasks/**`, `specs/**` and `reviews/*.md` as hard STOPs — the guard's actual aim (a live drain or concurrent task owns the tree) is untouched. `f1406-1` was repaired and re-dispatched as DISPATCH 2 under CLAUDE.md §7.5 (changed premise: only the pre-flight moved; scope is byte-identical). ⓘ **Recorded UNVERIFIED, deliberately: I could not establish who restored those 26 files.** They are clean now; no stash from tonight, no commit touches `artifacts/` since `76f7e565`, and neither `lane-runner-v3.sh` (which commits `artifacts` for lanes/art only, `:104`, and never for main, `:93`) nor `fire-runner.sh` contains a discard. A tracked surface that reverts itself with no record is worth one command from the next fire that sees it dirty. 🧹 **SIBLING SWEEP DONE, so nobody re-opens it: §3 of that skill holds exactly THREE pre-flight templates — LANE (had the exception), MAIN (fixed here), ART (has no git pre-flight at all, by design). The exposure was one template, and it is closed.** ⓘ No live master is exposed: the only queued item on the board is the repaired `f1406-1` itself. **GATE: none — cure landed in the template, in the master, and swept.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:689:✅ **f1405-1-land-the-cross-engine-wave-scaling-cure SHIPPED s1406 — eaefdb24308067d2ad28e6cc2e11cf86ed5469e1 — the sim stops inheriting V8's `Math.pow`.** All five sim-reachable `Math.pow(base, wave)` sites in `WaveSystem.ts` now use a file-local `scalePerWave` repeated-multiplication helper (spawn speed, spawn HP, trickle interval, baron component HP, baron component speed), because IEEE-754 `*` is exactly specified where `Math.pow` precision is implementation-defined. Closes the F-1404-2 causal chain and unblocks the twin-banks re-land (E1 driver 4 of 5) and the baron (5 of 5). 🔑 **THE CURE IS PROVEN AGAINST A SUBJECT THAT ACTUALLY DIVERGED — WHICH THE RUN ITSELF NEVER MEASURED.** The run reported only `the-claim`, whose hash **already agreed across engines before the cure**, so its own evidence table was compatible with the cure doing nothing for determinism (F-1406-3). s1406 measured **all three** contracts `HeadlessContractSim` supports, on both interpreters, with the pre-cure arm taken in a **detached worktree**: `e1-dry-gulch` `9de5c985`/`9de5c985` → unchanged · `the-claim` `02561b7f` both → `b1eeb320` both · **`e1-night-shift` `c832307e` (Node 26) vs `ed5d8203` (Node 23) → `30373c0b` on BOTH.** ✓ Reproduced **3/3 per engine** (an unreproducible pin would be a broken instrument, not a finding). ⚠️ **This corrects an inherited claim:** `reviews/f1404-1-cross-engine-wave-scaling-stop.md:33` states *"Main is not currently cross-engine divergent; the divergence is only observable once a contract long enough to reach wave 13 is present"* — **false as of `c2981ad3`**; `e1-night-shift` is a main-side contract needing no graft. The twin-banks graft was never the only divergent subject, only the one anybody had pointed a hash at. 🧾 **Gates:** tsc clean · build green · `gr-sim.test.mjs` **6/6/0 on Node 26.4.0 AND 6/6/0 on Node 23.11.1** · `test:node-guards` **230/230/0, zero skipped** · adjacent e2e ×6 at `--workers=1`: **10 reds, ALL fingerprint-matched by a CONTROL run of the same specs on the pre-cure tree in a detached worktree — identical 5 tests × 2 projects, so pre-existing and not caused.** Outcome invariants unchanged on both engines; `kills` 140→137 (2.1%), accepted per the master's scope 6; `Balance.ts` untouched. ⚖️ **OWNER VETO WINDOW OPEN (CLAUDE.md §7.4)** — re-baselining bench pins is reversible with one revert. ⚠️ **Sequencing unchanged: lane-c (`lane/e2-arsenal`) HOLDS `WaveSystem.ts`; the baron re-graft and twin-banks re-land must FOLLOW this merge, never reset over it.** Evidence reviews/f1405-1-cross-engine-wave-scaling-cure.md. **GATE: none.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:698:🔺 **F-1404-2 (s1404, MEASURED AND PROVEN AT THE ULP LEVEL — the sim’s determinism rests on `Math.pow`, whose precision ECMA-262 leaves to the implementation; 5 sim-reachable sites, not 1, and the NEXT slice to land uses one of them).** The f1403-1 run diagnosed the twin-banks hash divergence and ruled scope 5(a); the s1404 gate reproduced it end-to-end and proved the mechanism one level deeper. **The discriminating experiment — one tree, one directory, zero edits between runs, only the interpreter changed:** `node --test scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` gives **7 pass / 0 fail, `fnv1a32:5f57f7be`** under **Node 23.11.1** (the runner’s node) and **6 pass / 1 fail, `fnv1a32:bfd79d2a`** under **Node 26.4.0** (the fire shell’s node). **The primitive itself diverges:** `Math.pow(1.115, 3)` = `1.386195875` on Node 26 and `1.3861958749999999` on Node 23 — 1 ULP. Waves 1, 2, 4, 5, 13 and 20 agree; wave 3 is where the two V8 versions round differently, which is exactly the wave the run reached independently from the replay dump. Full causal chain, every link verified: V8 `Math.pow` differs 1 ULP at wave 3 → `hpScale` differs → `Enemy.spawn` stores the unrounded product (`34.93213605` vs `34.932136050000004`) → a lethal hit lands one tick differently at wave 13 → replay event **662** differs (`enemy_killed` vs `hero_damaged`) → the event-log hash differs. ✓ **VERIFIED BY READING**: `WaveSystem.ts:582` passes raw `Math.pow`, `Enemy.ts:599-600` stores it unrounded. ⚠️ **The run named ONE site; there are FIVE in sim-reachable code** — `WaveSystem.ts:579` speedScale · `:582` hpScale · `:744` trickleInterval · `:838` waveHpScale · `:839` waveSpeedScale (the other two `Math.pow` hits, `Vfx.ts:230` and `Game.ts:8009`, are render-side easing and are out of scope). **`:838`/`:839` are the BARON’s component path, and the baron is E1 driver 5 of 5 — the next thing queued to land.** It would fail the same way for the same reason, and a boss with many components has more chances to flip a comparison than twin-banks did; fixing this first prevents a fifth failed re-land. ⚠️ **The other bench pins are green by luck, not by design:** every contract runs the same shared `WaveSystem.spawnAtPosition`, so the divergent HP value enters every contract’s sim at wave 3 — the other six tests agree across both interpreters only because the 1-ULP difference never flips a comparison in those runs. **The E1 bench is a determinism certificate whose subject is not deterministic**; twin-banks is simply the first run long enough to expose it. ✅ **THE CURE WAS VERIFIED BEFORE IT WAS PROPOSED:** replacing `Math.pow(base, wave)` with repeated multiplication is bit-identical across engines because IEEE-754 `*` **is** exactly specified where `Math.pow` is not — 63 values (3 bases × waves 0..20) came back **IDENTICAL** on both interpreters, and `1.115^3` = `1.386195875`. No epsilon, no tolerance, no balance change (~1e-16). Evidence reviews/f1403-1-twin-banks-hash-divergence.md. **GATE: cure queued — tasks/f1404-1-make-the-wave-scaling-cross-engine-deterministic.md, authored + leaf-registered s1404.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:704:🔺 **F-1400-2 (s1400, MEASURED — TWIN-BANKS HELD: its own determinism gate fails at its own tip) ⛔ SUPERSEDED by F-1403-1 (s1403): the value is confirmed, but the "stale pin / late edit after measuring" CAUSE is refuted by measurement — the runner's greens are real and post-date its last edit. Do not act on the cause stated below.** `lane-headless-twin-banks` (lane/m3 tip e1bff1e8) was gated and REFUSED. scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs:222 pins the secure-run hash fnv1a32:5f57f7be; **measured fnv1a32:bfd79d2a**. Every other outcome field matches the run report exactly (secured:true, waves:20, timeMs:600000, kills:189, calls:0) and the idle hash bdd90123 passes — only the secure event-log hash differs. **Control proves it is lane-side, not mine and not my shell:** the same value came back in a detached scratch worktree at the lane tip AND inside lane-a's OWN worktree with its OWN node_modules, and lane-a is `git status` CLEAN at e1bff1e8 — so the runner measured this exact tree. Two directories, two processes, one value: stable, not flaky. The run report claims "GR-SIM 6/6" and also says "Review gap fixed", i.e. a late edit after measuring — the likely origin of a stale pin. **Not environmental:** advanceToTurn() is a pure fixed-step loop bounded by maxTicks and performance.now() only accumulates advanceCpuMs for diagnostics, never affecting control flow, so the fire shell CPU ceiling (F-1269-1) cannot move this hash. ⚠️ **On the MERGED tree this defect is INVISIBLE** — F-1400-1 throws first and an early assertion disables everything after it, so a fire that fixed only the call sites and did not re-run would have merged a false determinism gate. Branch INTACT, nothing lost. Evidence reviews/e1-headless-bench-twin-banks-baron-s1400.md. **GATE: cure merged — tasks/f1400-1-twin-banks-rebase-and-repin.md, authored + leaf-registered s1400.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:706:🔺 **F-1400-3 (s1400, MEASURED — BARON HELD: merged onto current main it INFINITE-LOOPS the escort headless run).** `lane-headless-baron` (lane/e2-arsenal tip 9a9fb2bb) was gated and REFUSED. On the merged tree the full gr-sim file never terminates — `node --test` runs with **--test-timeout=0**, so there is no bound; killed manually at 12 min, then again at 300 s. Process forensics named the culprit exactly: pid 88372 `node scripts/gr-sim.mjs --contract e2-hill-mine --seed e2-escort-headless --mode escort` at **99.4% CPU** for 6+ minutes — a spinning loop, not slowness. **Control, identical command and seed: clean main exits rc=0 in seconds** with {"secured":true,"waves":12,...,"eventLogHash":"fnv1a32:b3706fdc"}; **baron-merged is SIGKILLed at 90 s.** So the slice regresses e2-hill-mine escort mode — the very slice s1399 landed one fire earlier — and it is NOT a consequence of F-1400-1, since it reproduces with the call sites already fixed. **The runner could not have seen it:** its base 67d28607 predates 372808f0, so escort mode did not exist in its tree; its "GR-SIM 6/6" was true of its base and is false of main. ⓘ The baron's OWN measurements are sound — with only the F-1400-1 rewrite applied, the headline test passes in 12.4 s and its pinned hashes reproduce. **Suspected but UNVERIFIED (stated as hypothesis, not finding):** e2-hill-mine declares BOTH a baron block (escortCount:6) and an escort mode, and the slice threads a new escortsSpawned count through spawnBaronWave / spawnComponentBossWave / onBaronSpawned. Branch INTACT. Evidence reviews/e1-headless-bench-twin-banks-baron-s1400.md. ⚠️ **HYPOTHESIS REFUTED s1401 — the escortsSpawned suspicion stated above is WRONG and must not be inherited; see F-1401-1 below for the proven mechanism.** ✅ **CURED s1410 — `e45cf7c5`.** The driver can no longer spin (a `secureWave + 2` ceiling inside the loop, exiting non-zero with a diagnostic), so the symptom this row describes — a hand-killed 12-minute battery — cannot recur for any contract that fails to auto-secure. **GATE: CLOSED — cure merged as `e45cf7c5`, reviews/f1401-1-bound-the-headless-driver.md.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:708:🔺 **F-1401-1 (s1401, PROVEN BY THREE-ARM CONTROL — F-1400-3 diagnosed; the baron does not regress escort, it exposes a divergence).** s1400 asked the next fire to confirm its escortsSpawned hypothesis by reading rather than assuming. Read: **REFUTED.** The WaveSystem diff is a pure count pass-through that accumulates escortsSpawned from existing spawnAt return values and hands it to two callbacks — no loop, no effect on control flow, cannot spin. **The real mechanism, three arms, same command and seed, one detached worktree each:** clean main exits rc=0 in **4.5s** with eventLogHash fnv1a32:b3706fdc (reproducing the s1400 control exactly, which is what licenses the comparison) · baron-merged **never terminates**, alive past 150s · baron-merged with ONLY the Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER branch neutralised exits rc=0 in **4.57s**. So the cause is the slice adding autoSecureWaveForRun to HeadlessContractSim, returning Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER while a baron is declared and unbeaten; RunManager.ts:540 consumes it, the run never auto-secures, and scripts/gr-sim.mjs line 40 has an unbounded while loop. advanceToTurn own maxTicks guard never trips because it returns early on every wave change. ⚠️ **AND THE SLICE IS PROBABLY RIGHT, which is why this is not a revert.** Production gates the same thing on waitsForBaronDefeat (Game.ts:4709), which for e2-hill-mine returns **true** — its baron carries no variantId (the string variantId appears nowhere in the E2 contracts file), so the predicate falls through to the dynamo_crawler comparison and yields true. If that reading holds, the baron makes the headless sim AGREE with production, and it is main escort bench — asserting secured:true, waves:12 — that has been asserting an outcome production would not produce. **Read-verified, not run-verified; confirming it is scope item 3 of the master.** Evidence reviews/f1401-1-baron-escort-nontermination.md. ✅ **RULED AND CURED s1410 — `e45cf7c5`, and the read-verified half above is now INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED rather than inherited.** The drain re-derived it from source instead of trusting either the master or the runner: `e2-hill-mine`'s `twist.baron` exists at wave 12 and carries **no `variantId` key** (`"variantId" in baron` → **false**; the token appears **nowhere** in `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json`), so `Game.ts:4709 waitsForBaronDefeat()` falls through to `baron.variantId !== 'dynamo_crawler'` → **true**, and `autoSecureWaveForRun()` (`Game.ts:4673-4680`) returns `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`. **Production withholds. The reading holds; scope 3 ruled (a).** Main's bench had been asserting `cli.status === 0` / `secured:true` — an outcome the real game will not produce — and is re-based onto `cli.signal === null`, i.e. *the driver terminated on its own*, which is true today and after the baron lands. **GATE: CLOSED — cure merged as `e45cf7c5`, reviews/f1401-1-bound-the-headless-driver.md.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:712:🟢 **F-1400-1 (s1400, MEASURED — CLASS: a constructor change on main silently breaks every stale-based lane's .mjs call sites, invisibly to git AND to tsc).** s1399's 372808f0 changed HeadlessContractSim from positional `constructor(readonly contractId: string, readonly seed: string)` to an object `constructor(readonly boot: HeadlessContractBoot)`. **Both** waiting lanes branched before it and add new call sites in the OLD form — scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs:210,237 (twin-banks) and :220,281 (baron as merged). The defect survives every gate that runs before execution: **git merges it cleanly** (the ctor and the callers are in different files, so there is no conflict to resolve) and **`tsc --noEmit` is blind** (the callers are .mjs, loaded at runtime via vite.ssrLoadModule) — tsc was CLEAN on both merged trees. At runtime the string is taken as the boot object, so boot.contractId is undefined: `Error: Unknown contract: undefined`. **This is graft work, not a lane failure** — adapting a caller to a signature main changed is exactly what a 3-way graft is for — and it is filed as a CLASS because it will hit every lane still based before 372808f0. **Proven curable:** the 2-line rewrite alone makes the baron headline test pass with its hashes reproducing. 💡 The lesson generalises the s1301 family one step further: that law names ledger rows, law surfaces and gate topology as what a fire mutates late in its own run, and F-1399-2 added the code that law surfaces point INTO — this adds **the untyped callers that a typed signature change cannot reach.** Evidence reviews/e1-headless-bench-twin-banks-baron-s1400.md. **GATE: none — folded into the twin-banks cure; the next lane based before 372808f0 needs the same graft.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:718:⚖️ **RULED s1421 — THE LANE-B GRAFT: "THE CHEAPEST REAL MERGE ON THE BOARD" IS NOT A MERGE AT ALL. NOTHING ON lane-b IS FIRE-GRAFTABLE, AND TWO-THIRDS OF IT LANDED BY ANOTHER ROAD A DAY AGO.** Carried as the #1 or #3 next-fire priority by **four consecutive fires (s1417, s1418, s1419, s1420)**, each describing it as *"the cheapest real merge on the board"* and *"a cheap, well-lit job."* s1421 took the ruling and measured it. `lane/m4` is `ahead=3 behind=553`, `paths=14`, **13 residue lines across 7 paths** (s1419's count, reproduced exactly). The three ahead-commits decompose completely: ① **`cce99524` `lane-headless-the-claim`** — its content is **ALREADY ON MAIN**, re-landed as `e1-headless-the-claim-reland` and drained **s1392 `8e20d8ca`** (leaf `merged`, `merge-base --is-ancestor` ✓). ② **`c876f675` `lane-claim-geometry-declared`** — likewise, re-landed as `e1-claim-geometry-declared-reland`, drained **s1394 `a3e199f4`** (leaf `merged`, ancestor ✓); its exclusive paths sit at **zero residue** (`contracts.json` 0/33, `ContractFamilies.ts` 0/20, `Terrain.ts` 0/7). ③ **`7c4f132f` `f1328-1-drill-yard-census-debt`** — **BLOCKED, `blockClass: "disputed"`**, which per **F-1383-1** is treated as `owner-fork` until an attended session rules: the STOP is total, do not gate. 🔑 **The 13 lines split exactly two ways, and neither way is a fire's to take.** **Five are SUPERSEDED**, verified line-by-line against main rather than inferred: the lane's positional `new HeadlessContractSim('the-claim', 'e1-the-claim-01')` vs main's object form at `gr-sim.test.mjs:157`; `kills: 140` vs main's `137` at `:172`; `eventLogHash: 'fnv1a32:02561b7f'` vs main's `b1eeb320` at `:174`; `{ now: () => … }` which main **absorbed and extended** with `storage: HEADLESS_META_STORAGE` (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:250`); and a README line where **main lists four contracts to the lane's three**. **The remaining eight all trace to the BLOCKED commit** — attributed by reading the hunks, not by guessing: both `agent-view.spec.ts` residue lines (*"all six E1 mechanics manifests"* and the six-element `toEqual`) are `7c4f132f`'s own `five → six` edits, while `c876f675`'s additions to that same file (the `center-ford` / `water_crossings` lines) are fully absorbed; `072-era-activation` (1), `e1-baron` (2) and the `e1-drill-yard` fixture block (3) are the same six-contract/drill-yard census. ⚠️ **This is the *absent-from-main ≠ unseen-by-main* hazard at full scale: superseded content and re-landed content both read exactly like unabsorbed content in a residue count, and a residue count is a one-directional measure that cannot tell you which.** The tool was right about every number and the four-fire framing built on it was still wrong. 💡 **And my own first hypothesis here was ALSO wrong, which is the reusable half:** `drain-block-check lane/m4` returned **UNKNOWN**, and neither upper commit's task name matched a leaf — I was one edit from filing *"two ahead-commits have no goal leaf"* as a Goal Registration Law finding. The leaves exist under **`*-reland` ids**; the bookkeeping was never missing, my lookup key was. *A fresh classifier's first hit is probably its own bug — fourth consecutive fire in which that has paid out.* ➡️ **RULING: do NOT graft, do NOT reset, do NOT carry this as a pending merge again.** lane-b is archivable the moment the owner rules on the disputed leaf, and not one minute before; the standing 🚫 DO-NOT-RESET order remains correct and is now correct *for a stated reason*. The owner-facing residue of this whole thread is **F-1396-4** (carve the uncontested files out of `7c4f132f`) — unchanged, still one word. **GATE: owner ruling on `f1328-1-drill-yard-census-debt` (`blockClass: disputed`); no fire action owed.**
