tasks/BACKLOG.md:863:✅ **SHIPPED s1417 — `f1415-1-guard-the-component-boss-secure-branch` MERGED at `cf005d5973ead015d273a8be77efa6a7de0b597a`. F-1415-1 CURED: the component-boss branch now has a guard, and the guard was AIMED before it was trusted.** The predicate that `1a4831df` cured lived inside an event-handler closure, and F-1415-2 had **retired the only end-to-end probe that could reach it** — so there was no runnable path to the branch from outside, which is precisely why a read had been standing in for a guard. The run extracts it as an exported pure `bossKillSecuresRun(baron, contractId, event)` in `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` and pins it with `scripts/component-boss-secure.test.mjs` (5 cases), rooted in `test:node-guards` (roster **42 → 43**). ✓ **The extraction is behaviour-identical, verified by READING the diff rather than inferring it from the green**: the moved body is character-for-character the prior inline expression with `this.contractId` replaced by the parameter. ⭐ **RED PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING THE DEFECT (the s1299/s1300 standard):** dropping the `bossRemaining === 0` conjunct in a scratch copy reddened `E2 default railcar group secures only when its last component dies` with **`true !== false`**, **4 pass / 1 fail**. A guard green on both the broken and the fixed tree certifies its own aim, not the fix. 🔢 **Both sub-branches are covered, which was s1416's whole point** (F-1415-3's lesson about counting rather than asserting): the **railcar** suffix (`e2-hill-mine`/`e2-trestle`/`e2-incline` — components, no `variantId`) **and** the **component-boss** suffix (`e3-canyon-works`/`e4-dust-flats`/`e5-deepwater-claim`/`e6-glow-mesa`), plus the plain-Baron no-group path and an elite-kind mismatch case. 🧾 **Gates, all re-measured in the fire shell:** `npx tsc --noEmit` **rc 0** · `npm run build` **1.19 s** · own guard **5 pass / 0 fail** · `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` **8 pass / 0 fail** (unchanged 8/8) · `test:node-guards` **253 tests, 250 pass, 0 fail, 3 skipped** (the documented F-1408-2 fire-shell cross-engine skips). **No Playwright, and that is justified rather than skipped:** the diff touches the headless bench, `package.json` (one alphabetical guard entry) and one new test file — `src/game/` is untouched, so no rendering or player-facing surface changed. 🔒 **THE FIREWALL HELD, AND IT IS THE MOST VALUABLE THING ABOUT THIS RUN:** the master ordered a STOP if the runner began trying to green the **retired** escort probe — **two prior fires died exactly there** — and this run left it untouched and said so explicitly. Review `reviews/f1415-1.md`. **GATE: none — shipped.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:865:🔺 **F-1417-3 (s1417, MEASURED — TWO FROZEN LANES HELD NOTHING BUT SUPERSEDED CONTENT, AND THE FILE-LEVEL VERDICT COULD NOT SAY SO.)** s1416 left `lane-a` and `lane-c` reading **HOLDS** and standing orders said *do not reset*. Asked at line level with `scripts/lane-absorbed-lines.mjs`, the residue is **8 lines total and every one is an older form main has already moved past**. `lane-a` (`lane/m3`): `assets/contracts/bench-seeds.json` fully ABSORBED; `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` ABSORBED token-level; `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` held 5 lines — `kills: 189` and `eventLogHash: 'fnv1a32:5f57f7be'` (**pre-cure twin-banks values that `eaefdb24` moved to `176` / `d5895547`**, both on s1414's explicit do-not-paste list), two `new HeadlessContractSim('e1-twin-banks', …)` **positional** constructor calls superseded by main's object form, and an AP-07 support-list assertion that main has since **widened** with `e1-baron`. `lane-c` (`lane/e2-arsenal`): `bench-seeds.json` and `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts` **fully ABSORBED** (so s1416's carried *"lane-c additionally needs the WaveSystem re-graft"* was already discharged); the 3 residual lines are two positional constructor calls plus **`if (event.type === 'enemy_killed' && event.eliteKind === 'baron') this.postBaronDefeat(event.at);`** — the **pre-cure single-string predicate that F-1414-1 named as the root cause and `1a4831df` fixed**. Verified against `git show main:src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:399-401`, which carries the cured component-aware form. 🔑 **The transferable half: `BOTH-MOVED` is a triage bucket, not a loss verdict, and "absent from main" is not "unseen by main" — content main deliberately SUPERSEDED reads identically to content main never saw.** The one-directional line question distinguishes them; the file-level one cannot. ⓘ Both tips archived to permanent refs **and pushed to origin before any reset**, so the act is lossless and reversible: `archive/lane-m3-s1417-superseded-e1bff1e8`, `archive/lane-e2-arsenal-s1417-superseded-9a9fb2bb`. Both lanes now measure `ahead=0 behind=0` — **fully current, not merely usable.** Fleet: **lane-a / lane-c / lane-d USABLE, lane-b still HOLDS** (14 paths, incl. two LANE-ONLY e2e specs — genuinely unabsorbed, do not reset). **GATE: none — ruled and cured.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:871:✅ **SHIPPED s1415 — `f1414-1-cure-the-component-boss-secure-gate` MERGED at `1a4831df70ad49aa8fae6e371cbd263ecbaa639b`. THE E1 BENCH CLOSES AT 5/5, and the run that produced it had STOPPED.** The main-slot run reported **STOP — not READY-FOR-GATES** and deliberately declined the battery, because the master’s scope-4 escort canary stayed **rc 1** after the cure. ⭐ **Its reasoning was sound and its premise was false** (F-1415-2 below): that command is in no test file. s1415 ran the battery the run declined, on the run’s own preserved output (`archive/f1414-1-baron-cure-s1415` = `aa519ac7`, restored by path-scoped checkout, four files). 🧾 **Gates, all re-measured in the fire shell:** `npx tsc --noEmit` **rc 0** · `npm run build` **1.25 s** · `node --test scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` **8 pass / 0 fail / 53.8 s**, against a **clean-main control of 7/7 taken before the graft** — the battery count moved 7→8, exactly the one test this diff adds · `bench-seeds` + `cross-engine-skip` **5/5** · `test:node-guards` **240 tests, 237 pass, 0 fail, 3 skipped** (the documented F-1408-2 fire-shell cross-engine skips, which print their own “this green is NOT coverage” banner) · `npx playwright test e2e/e2-rail-tough-diagonal.spec.ts e2e/_s106-prospector-boot-probe.spec.ts --workers=1` **4 passed / 33.0 s**, desktop **and** 390 px, zero console/page errors. 🔑 **The predicate’s correctness was established BY READING, not by inheriting the run’s unpreserved diagnostic:** `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:854-855` and the cured sim build the **same group-id expression**, and `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:794` returns early unless `wave === baron.wave`, so the sim’s `baron.wave` and the runtime `wave` are provably the same number. `src/game/Game.ts` was **not touched** (`git diff --stat` empty), which is what makes the parity argument load-bearing rather than circular. Both `gate-side` leaves lifted by the fire that landed the cure, no owner word owed or spent: `f1414-1…` → merged, `e1-headless-baron` → merged. `lane/e2-arsenal` stays **HOLDS** and unreset. Review `reviews/f1414-1.md`. **GATE: none — shipped.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:873:🔺 **F-1415-2 (s1415, MEASURED — THE “ESCORT CANARY” WAS NEVER A CANARY, AND THE GREEN IT DEMANDED ENCODED THE DIVERGENCE IT WAS SUPPOSED TO CATCH.)** Two consecutive main-slot runs — `f1413-1` and `f1414-1` — STOPPED because `node scripts/gr-sim.mjs --contract e2-hill-mine --mode escort --policy=idle` stayed **rc 1** (`wave=15 ceiling=14`). ⚠️ **That command appears in NO test file.** The pinned escort test is `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs:89`, and it asserts exactly two things: `assert.equal(cli.signal, null)` — which **rc 1 satisfies**, since a process that exits 1 is not signal-killed — and that the first stdout line carries `modes[0].id === "escort"`. It has **never** asserted `rc 0` and has **never** asserted `secured`. ✓ **Proven, not argued: the whole suite is 8/8 green on the grafted tree with that probe red.** 🔑 **And the green the two masters demanded was the bug.** The pre-graft control (`rc 0`, wave 12, `secured: true`, `fnv1a32:5ad506eb`) is the headless sim **auto-securing past a live Armored Railcar** — while `src/game/Game.ts:4673-4679` (`autoSecureWaveForRun` → `waitsForBaronDefeat()`, `:4709-4714`), **on clean main and untouched by this slice**, has always withheld auto-secure until the baron is beaten. The slice cures that divergence; the probe measured it and called it correct. Under `--policy=idle` the driver issues no orders at all, so it can never kill a 3-part boss at `hpScale: 30`, and the F-1401-1 ceiling is the correct terminus. ⭐ **The `f1414-1` run saw this more clearly than either master and refused to paper over it, verbatim from its report: “such a bypass would hide the production behavior difference rather than prove the requested component-destruction cure.”** It was right to refuse the bypass; it was wrong only about what that implied for the merge. ⚖️ **RULING: the probe is RETIRED as an acceptance test. Its red is expected. Do not re-open this hunt, and do not “fix” it.** This also answers the question `f1401-1` left open — *whether the e2-hill-mine escort bench should assert `secured: true` at all* — **it should not.** **GATE: none — ruled.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:875:✅ **F-1415-1 CLOSED — cured `cf005d597`, RETIRED s1482 as a GHOST LINE (Mistake #5).** The cure shipped and this row kept reading 🟡 open for three days. **Verified s1482 by file-probe, not by grepping commit messages (Mistake #16):** `scripts/component-boss-secure.test.mjs` EXISTS, `git merge-base --is-ancestor cf005d597 main` returns 0, and `package.json`'s `test:node-guards` names it — so the gate's own condition ("closed when that test lands in `test:node-guards`") is met. It covers exactly what the REC asked: the component branch both ways (`bossRemaining: 0` -> true, `1` -> false), wrong-group rejection, the E3 `component-boss` suffix variant, and elite-kind mismatch. ⓘ A grep of `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` looks empty because the cure landed in its own file, which is how this row stayed invisible. HISTORY: `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs`’s new baron test covers the **plain-baron** path only (`e1-baron`: `secured: true`, one `baron_defeated`, rocket telegraph/volley, the escorts-capped case) — that path is green and now pinned. The **component** path (`bossGroupId` match **and** `bossRemaining === 0`) is exercised by **no test**. The only evidence it fires is the run’s high-power Hill Mine diagnostic (component remaining `2 → 1 → 0`, secured at wave 12, exactly one defeat event), which was **not preserved as anything runnable**. s1415 verified the group-id link by reading both construction sites (see the SHIPPED row), which is why the merge stands — **but a read is not a guard.** Blast radius if it is wrong is small and bounded: headless `e2-hill-mine` runs would never secure, no pinned bench asserts them, and the game path is untouched. **REC: a test that spawns the railcar group and kills its three parts. Fire-authorable, no spec fork.** **GATE: SATISFIED at `cf005d597` — retired s1482.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:877:🟡 **F-1415-3 (s1415, MEASURED — two facts stated as verified in the `f1414-1` master are wrong; neither changed the diagnosis.)** The master’s WHY and s1414’s F-1414-1 both assert `e2-hill-mine` declares *“a five-part `components` array”* and *“`secureWave: 12`”*. Read from `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json`: the array has **three** parts — `wheels`, `boiler`, `cabin` — and the contract has **no top-level `secureWave` at all**; the 12 is `twist.baron.wave`. The eliteKind chain holds regardless of either number, and the run’s own trace said *“all three railcar components alive”*, which is the correct count. Recorded because both were asserted under a ✓ and neither had been counted. **GATE: none — closed by this row and by `reviews/f1414-1.md`.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:881:⏹️ **STOPPED + SUPERSEDED s1414 — `f1413-1-baron-reland-on-cured-main` refused itself at its own canary, which is the outcome the master was written to produce.** The run took a pre-graft escort control **before** touching the tree (**rc 0**, 4.55 s, wave 12, `secured: true`, `fnv1a32:5ad506eb`), grafted, re-ran the identical command (**rc 1**, 6.00 s, `gr-sim wave ceiling exceeded: contract=e2-hill-mine mode=escort seed=gold-rush wave=15 ceiling=14`), and STOPPED. `npx tsc --noEmit` rc 0 on the grafted tree; build and guard batteries deliberately NOT run after the stop — evidence gathered past a STOP only builds a case toward merging what the canary just refused. ✓ **s1413’s epistemic call is now MEASURED, not argued: a bound converts a hang into a red; it does not prove the behaviour change is gone.** `e45cf7c5`’s ceiling is exactly what let this run see the cause in five minutes instead of spinning at 99.4% CPU — the bound was the right act AND the cause survived it, both at once. ⓘ **CUSTODY (fire.md §3.0b): the four modified files were NOT left in main’s working tree.** They are preserved at `save/f1413-1-baron-graft-s1414` = **`41065da7`** (+260/−10) and main was returned clean — `git status` over `src/ scripts/ assets/` empty, `npx tsc --noEmit` **rc 0**. `lane/e2-arsenal` (`9a9fb2bb`) is untouched and remains the upstream salvage-ref: **RE-GRAFT, NEVER RESET.** Review `reviews/f1413-1.md`. **GATE: none — superseded by `f1414-1`.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:882:🔺 **F-1414-1 (s1414, VERIFIED AT SOURCE — the cause of F-1400-3, named at last: THE SECURE GATE WAITS FOR A STRING THE CONTRACT NEVER EMITS.)** The predecessor run named this cause; I did not inherit it, I read the code, and it holds in four links. **(1)** The grafted gate keys on the mere PRESENCE of a baron block — `autoSecureWaveForRun: () => this.manifest.twist.baron && !this.baronBeaten ? Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER : …` — so any contract with a truthy `twist.baron` can never auto-secure until `baronBeaten` flips. **(2)** `baronBeaten` flips on exactly one string: `if (event.type === "enemy_killed" && event.eliteKind === "baron") this.postBaronDefeat(event.at)`. **(3)** `e2-hill-mine` declares `bossKind: "railcar"`, `secureWave: 12`, `escortCount: 6` and a five-part `components` array, and `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:866` spawns every part with `eliteKind: baron.bossKind ?? "railcar"` — so `"baron"` is **never emitted**. **(4)** Therefore `baronBeaten` can never become true, auto-secure is withheld forever, and the run overruns `secureWave: 12` into the ceiling at wave 15. ⚠️ **THE OBVIOUS ONE-LINE CURE IS WRONG AND MUST NOT BE APPLIED BLIND:** `bossRemaining === 0` alone OVER-FIRES, because `bossGroupId` is written by **five** systems — `WaveSystem.ts:880`, `SalvageClawBossSystem.ts:365`, `OldDiggerBossSystem.ts:428`, `HomemakerBossSystem.ts:388`, `DredgeQueenBossSystem.ts:390` — so keying on group-death alone would let an unrelated boss group’s last kill secure a baron contract. ✓ `degradeBossGroup` (`src/entities/pools.ts:732-745`) was read and IS sound: `remaining` excludes the killed enemy and counts only the living, so `remaining === 0` genuinely means the last component died. **REC: tie the kill to the contract’s OWN declared `bossKind` and require the group down; make 3a/3b/3c explicit rulings rather than assumptions.** **GATE: CURED when `f1414-1` lands with the canary red reproduced BEFORE it is proven green.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:886:✅ **AUTHORED s1414, DISPATCHED + SHIPPED `1a4831df` (drained s1415) — label corrected s1418, it had read "NOT YET DISPATCHED" after the event** — `f1414-1-cure-the-component-boss-secure-gate`: cures F-1414-1 and finishes E1 driver 5 of 5, closing the E1 bench at 5/5.** Re-grafts from `save/f1413-1-baron-graft-s1414` (`41065da7`) **as a patch, never a branch merge**, cures the predicate, and gates. ✓ **The block on `e1-headless-baron` is still `blockClass: gate-side`, NOT `owner-fork`** — no owner word lifts it and it must not reach Robin’s desk; a fire lifts it by landing the cure. 🔑 **Central order — the runner MUST reproduce the canary RED before claiming it green.** A canary green on both the broken tree and the fixed one certifies its own aim, not the fix (the s1299/s1300 standard); a non-reproducing red is a **STOP**, because it means the instrument is broken rather than the diagnosis. 🚫 **Second order — the obvious predicate over-fires** (F-1414-1: five systems write `bossGroupId`), so scope 3 makes **3a** (does the single-baron path still work — verify by RUNNING, not reasoning), **3b** (can any of the four non-`WaveSystem` boss systems emit a kill whose `eliteKind` equals the active contract’s `bossKind`), and **3c** (does the predicate defeat `postBaronDefeat`’s existing rollback by firing on the 2nd and 3rd component kill) explicit rulings the runner must answer in prose. ⚠️ **Third order — the pins are EVIDENCE here, not staleness** (F-1414-2): `869` / `b9566c6d` were re-derived 3/3 on two engines, so a *difference* is the thing that must be explained loudly, not a match. Carries forward the predecessor’s still-binding scopes: no raw checkout of `WaveSystem.ts` (would silently discard the `eaefdb24` `Math.pow` cure), second-engine derivation on **Node 23.11.1** (a fire shell structurally cannot produce it, F-1408-2), report-don’t-fix the `Balance.sparkRig` mutation, and **do not touch `tasks/goals.json`** (the leaf flip is the draining fire’s paired act, F-1384-1). All four `*BossSystem.ts` files are on the NO list as **read-for-ruling, edit-none**. Leaf registered in this same commit. **GATE: dispatch with `cp tasks/f1414-1-cure-the-component-boss-secure-gate.md tasks/queue/main/` and flip its leaf `queued`→`building`; re-verify `lane/e2-arsenal` is intact first — with `save/f1413-1-baron-graft-s1414` it is one of only two copies of the baron work.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:888:⛔ **AUTHORED s1413, DISPATCHED + STOPPED (superseded by f1414-1; DO NOT RE-QUEUE per standing orders) — label corrected s1418, it had read "NOT YET DISPATCHED", inviting exactly the re-queue the standing orders forbid** — `f1413-1-baron-reland-on-cured-main`: E1 driver 5 of 5, the FIRST boss driver, which closes the E1 bench at 5/5.** ✓ **The block on `e1-headless-baron` is `blockClass: gate-side`, NOT `owner-fork`** — `tasks/goals.json` says so verbatim (*"no owner word will lift this; a fire lifts it by landing the cure"*), so nothing here is waiting on Robin and it must not be carried to his desk. ✓ **VERIFIED s1413 BY READING THE COMMITS, NOT INHERITED:** F-1400-1 is mechanical (the lane branched at `67d28607`, predating `372808f0`, so both new call sites read `new HeadlessContractSim('e1-baron','e1-baron-01')` positionally — git merges it clean, tsc is blind, and s1400 proved that with only the 2-line rewrite the baron headline test PASSES); F-1400-3's mechanism was cured by **`e45cf7c5`**, whose own findings include **F-1410-3 "lane/e2-arsenal unblocked; RE-GRAFT, never reset"**; and `lane/e2-arsenal` measured this fire is ahead=1, behind=101, tracked-dirt=0, 4 files, **+260−10** vs merge-base `67d28607`, with `lane-usable.mjs` reporting **HOLDS** — hence a main-slot re-land, because a lane pre-flight would destroy the only copy. 🔍 **The master's central order is an epistemic one the inherited ledger does not make: A BOUND CONVERTS A HANG INTO A RED; IT DOES NOT PROVE THE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE IS GONE.** F-1400-3's finding was that merging this slice *changed what escort mode does* on `e2-hill-mine`, and `e45cf7c5` touched none of `spawnBaronWave` / `spawnComponentBossWave` / `onBaronSpawned` — it put a ceiling under the loop they were spinning. So the **symptom is bounded and the cause is UNVERIFIED**, and scope 3 turns that into a before/after escort control run the runner derives itself, with three explicit rulings and two STOP branches. 🚫 *