tasks/BACKLOG.md:1170:✅ **F-1326-1 (s1326, ✅ CLOSED IN THE SAME FIRE THAT FILED IT — the fold its GATE asked for was two edits to the file I had just drained, so I did it rather than leave a 🟡 to generate a dispatch. `e2e/charter-press-totality.spec.ts`: a dated four-line comment recording that the build-zone template search is LOAD-BEARING and naming probe D's consequence, plus the assertion message narrowed to *"…on a fresh charter of the build-zone template"* so it no longer claims more than it measures. Re-gated: tsc clean · totality 4/4 across desktop AND mobile · whole-suite collection still `2476 tests in 350 files`. ORIGINAL TEXT FOLLOWS — OPEN, NON-BLOCKING, COSMETIC — A CORRECT FINDING WITH THE WRONG VERB, AND THE MEASUREMENT THAT SHOWS BOTH HALVES).** F-1324-3 claimed a menu reorder would leave the old test *“passing while asserting nothing.”* ⚠️ **I ran the control and for the reorder I tested that is FALSE:** old spec (`git show 7d255a53:e2e/charter-press-totality.spec.ts`) against a rig with arms 3↔4 swapped goes **RED, loudly** — `Expected "blank:briefing.goal" / Received "illegal:spawn-edges-empty"`. The old test would have caught it. ✓ **But the finding was right about the CLASS, and here is the reachable silent path, measured rather than argued.** Probing every Frontier contract for build zones: `the-claim` **undefined** · `e1-drill-yard` **undefined** · `e1-dry-gulch` **undefined** · `e1-night-shift` **undefined** · `e1-twin-banks` **2** · `e1-baron` **undefined** — **only 1 of 6 has them, and it is not `templates[0]`, which is the template the test body actually runs.** So on `the-claim` the `illegal:zone-outside-claim` arm returns `'noop'` on a **fresh** charter; the old test's second assertion was `expect(arms[3]!()).toBe('noop')`, so **moving the zones arm to index 3 would have passed while asserting nothing whatever about the briefing guard.** My first reorder simply happened to hit the loud path instead of the quiet one. 💡 *The reusable half: “it would fail silently” is a claim about a **specific** reorder, and testing one reorder neither proves nor disproves it. The old test had two assertions and only one of them was fragile.* ⓘ **The residual defect itself is one line of wording.** `mutationArmIndices()` builds its map from the buildZones template precisely so `'noop'` never appears and the map stays injective (probe D: point it at `templates[0]` and the guard reds immediately — the search is **load-bearing**). But its assertion message reads *“mutation arm label "noop" must not occur on a fresh charter”*, which is true of `e1-twin-banks` and **false of the other five**, including the one under test. The assertion is sound where it is taken; the wording claims more than it measures, and a future reader could act on the wider reading. GATE: none owed — fold a one-line comment naming the template into the next touch of this rig.
